Package: MoCo
Title: Motion-Controlled Estimation of Group Differences in Brain Phenotypes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xiyan", "Tan",
           email = "xxx@emory.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jialu", "Ran", role = "aut"),
    person("Benjamin B.", "Risk", role = "aut"),
    person("David", "Benkeser", role = "aut"),
    person("Brain Research in Imaging Statistics Kit", role = "cph")
    )
Description: Implements nonparametric one-step estimators for group-specific
    brain-phenotype means and contrasts while accounting for motion-related
    selection, following Ran, Shultz, Risk and Benkeser (2026)
    <doi:10.1093/biomtc/ujag099>. Nuisance functions can be estimated with
    'SuperLearner', and conditional motion densities can be modeled with the
    highly adaptive lasso, log-normal generalized linear models, or generalized
    additive models for location, scale, and shape. Simultaneous confidence
    bands provide family-wise error-rate control across multiple outcomes.
